<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gyeongsun of Silla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 927–935</span> · <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gyeongsun was the last king of Silla, placed on the throne in 927 by the rebel leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyeon-hwon">Gyeon Hwon</a> of Later Baekje after the sack of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gyeongju">Gyeongju</a>. Ruling a kingdom reduced to its capital region, in 935 he surrendered peacefully to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taejo-of-goryeo">Wang Geon</a> of Goryeo, who gave him high rank and absorbed Silla's aristocracy. He died in 978.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gyeongsun-of-silla.jpg" alt="Gyeongsun of Silla" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: A painter in Goryeo dynasty · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_portait_of_Gyeongsun.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
